output: include cstdint for uint8_t

output.h uses uint8_t directly, so include the header that defines it instead
of relying on transitive includes from other standard headers.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>

--- a/include/woff2/output.h
+++ b/include/woff2/output.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cstring>
+#include <cstdint>
